  "id": "COMPOUND:11413 - PROTEIN:932",
  "verbalization": "Norgestrienone is implicated in the regulation of 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2B through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Norgestrienone interacts with the GABA(A) Receptor Benzodiazepine Binding Site, which in turn targets the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2B. This indicates a potential role in modulating the activity of the 5-HT2B receptor, possibly through a mechanism involving benzodiazepine-like ligands. Additionally, Norgestrienone is also shown to target 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 5A, which in turn targets the 5-HT2B receptor, suggesting a broader involvement in receptor regulation. The presence of multiple targets and the involvement of different receptor subtypes highlight the complexity of the relationship, with the 5-HT2B receptor being a central node in the network. The integration of these pathways underscores the potential for Norgestrienone to influence receptor function through a variety of mechanisms, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
